      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Why choose them: They are the most popular choice along the Wasatch Front (making up about 60% of local roofs) because of their affordable upfront cost and traditional look .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Utah performance: Modern 30-year architectural shingles handle standard snow loads well. Opting for Class 4 impact-resistant shingles can help protect against severe summer hailstorms and may qualify you for a discount on your homeowner's insurance ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The drawback: Intense UV exposure, high altitude, and freeze-thaw cycles mean asphalt shingles typically last around 20 years in Utah before needing replacement."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Metal Roofing in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Why choose them: Standing seam metal or stone-coated steel roofs are increasingly popular for higher-elevation and mountain properties (such as Heber City, Park City, and the canyons) ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Utah performance: Metal effortlessly sheds heavy mountain snow loads and ice, resists high-altitude UV degradation, and will not absorb water during freeze-thaw cycles. They also reflect solar heat, which helps with summer cooling.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The drawback: The initial installation cost is roughly 2 to 3 times higher than asphalt shingles, and installation requires specialized local contractors."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Which Should You Pick?"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose Asphalt Shingles if: You are on a tighter budget, plan to move or sell within the next 10 to 15 years, or prefer a classic neighborhood aesthetic ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose Metal Roofing if: You are building or staying in your \"forever home\" in a high-snow or high-wind area (like Heber/Park City) and want a 50-year solution that requires minimal long-term maintenance."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down the best fit, tell me:"
